# ── Large derived files: ship the gzipped copy, not the 79 MB original ────────
# Scripts prefer the plain CSV when present and fall back to the .gz, so a
# local uncompressed copy is fine — it just never enters version control.
data/reference/RNAseq_to_TF_Targets.csv
!data/reference/RNAseq_to_TF_Targets.csv.gz

# ── Retired: uncited G×E core analysis ────────────────────────────────────────
# 13_Supp_GxE_core_analysis.py (in-degree histogram + TF Jaccard heatmap) is not
# cited anywhere in the manuscript, and its output filenames collided with the
# real Figure 6 panels B and C. Excluded from the repository. Safe to delete
# from disk entirely; these rules can then go too:
#   rm scripts/13_Supp_GxE_core_analysis.py
#   rm outputs/supplementary/Figure6_*
scripts/13_Supp_GxE_core_analysis.py
outputs/supplementary/Figure6_panelB_GxE_indegree.*
outputs/supplementary/Figure6_panelC_TF_coregulation.*
outputs/supplementary/Figure6_GxE_core_stats.csv
outputs/supplementary/Figure6_GxE_per_gene_indegree.csv

